for the second day in a row a wreath  laid by a british minister outside the  kremlin walls the defense secretary with  his two top commanders in moscow to meet  his russian counterpart sergey shoigu  and the russian general chief of staff  it may well be that nothing comes of  this meeting the russians have been  pretty firm in their position that what  they do on their own territory is their  own business but at least there will  have been personal contacts made to the  two military men who have a direct line  to vladimir putin  [Music]  and if there was no breakthrough at  least a step in the right direction  what is incredibly important especially  at this time with over a hundred  thousand troops at high readiness on the  borders of another country is that we do  not get into a position of  miscalculation or escalation  and only through those type of  relationships and the ability to talk to  each other at times of concern  can we  pave the way for any de-escalatory  measures  as russia continues joint military  drills with belarus the u.s called an  urgent phone meeting with nato and eu  leaders  and warned again that an invasion could  come at any time  as we've said before  we are in the window when an invasion  could begin at any time should vladimir  putin decide to order it i will not  comment on the details of our  intelligence information but i do want  to be clear it could begin during the  olympics  despite a lot of speculation  that it would only happen after the  olympics  u.s citizens have been asked to leave  ukraine within the next 24 to 48 hours  and the uk has followed suit telling  british nationals to leave while  commercial means are still available  the u.s president making it clear that  he would not send in troops to save them  for fear of direct confrontation between  u.s and russian forces  that's a world war when americans and  russia start shooting at one another  we're in a very different world than  we've ever been in  sergey shoigu assured ben wallace as  russia has done over and over again that  he had no intention of invading ukraine  but it will be russia's actions not  words which count  dana magnay sky news moscow
 

